  "slug": "tumor-cell-28fd",
  "summary": "Recent single-cell and bulk transcriptomic studies dissect stromal and fibroblast programs in fibrotic and degenerative tissues.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is transcriptomic dissection of stromal and fibroblast compartments in fibrotic and degenerative tissue, using single-cell and bulk RNA-seq alongside integrative machine learning. In idiopathic subglottic stenosis, elevated EN1 and YAP/TAZ signaling in diseased subglottis accompanies fibroblast expression of COL1A1, COL3A1 and EN1, which verteporfin reduces in patient fibroblasts. Bulk profiling of normal versus glaucomatous trabecular meshwork cells on soft hydrogels identifies 588 DEGs spanning TGF-beta and Wnt fibrosis programs. Single-cell atlases of distal radius cartilage and knee osteoarthritis annotate cell types and oxidative stress-linked chondrocyte states, while keratoconus and mouse dry eye studies nominate biomarkers through LASSO, SVM-RFE, Scissor and CIBERSORTx. Darier disease fibroblast methylation links hub-gene changes to transcriptional direction. Novel contributions are mainly candidate biomarkers and cell-state maps rather than mechanistic proof.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-28"
}
